In this extended version of the model, I asked the machine to predict not only one year, but multiple future years.
This helps us see how temperature may continue increasing if current trends remain the same.
Higher temperature can make hurricanes stronger, droughts longer, and floods more damaging.

This version of the model does not just predict one future year — it predicts many future years like 2030, 2035, 2040, 2045, and 2050.
The model looks at how temperature has increased in the past and then guesses what future temperatures might be if the same pattern continues.

These future values help us understand that if temperature keeps rising, then extreme weather events like storms, floods, and droughts 
